  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP Protection and Development for Resilience in Jerusalem</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main goal of this project is to provide integrated support to enhance the Palestinian community&apos;s resilience in East Jerusalem. The project includes three outcomes; 1- Support Augusta Victoria Hospital with urgently needed medications and medical supplies needed mainly by cancer patients. 2. Support Palestinian legal organizations to help Palestinians living in Jerusalem obtain building licenses and preserve their housing rights. 3 Support small Palestinian tourist businesses, especially women and youth, and implement business development initiatives and entrepreneurship. Preserving the environment is interrelated mainly with outcome 2 by ensuring urban planning for new housing projects with no harm to the environment. Gender equality is more related to outcome 3- as Palestinian women&apos;s participation in the local economy and workforce is minimal.</narrative>
  </description>
